    "body": "<details><summary>AI feedback</summary>\n\nProposed fixes for defects D1 and D2 aren't applied yet.\n\nD1: In `download the hyperlink`, `subject`'s `hyperlink referrer policy` is read after `fire a download request navigate event` dispatches the `navigate` event, whereas `urlString` and `filename` are snapshotted before it (and `following hyperlinks` passes `hyperlink referrer policy` before `Navigate` fires `navigate`). If a `navigate` event listener mutates `e.sourceElement.referrerPolicy` or `e.sourceElement.rel`, `download the hyperlink` would use the mutated value; Safari Technology Preview and Chrome Canary both snapshot `referrerPolicy` before firing `navigate`. Not applied: proposed fix ([spec](https://github.com/noamr/html/commit/4e8682a), [test](https://github.com/noamr/wpt/commit/8051ec0)).\n\nD2: In `web-platform-tests/wpt#64051`, `resources/download-referrerpolicy.js` triggers multiple synthetic `element.click()` downloads in the same tab without user activation, causing `download-referrerpolicy.html` and `download-referrerpolicy-overrides-document-policy.html` to time out on the second download in Chrome Canary (`DownloadRequestLimiter` blocks the second automatic download behind a prompt, so `receive(id)` hangs). Not applied: [proposed fix](https://github.com/noamr/wpt/commit/7a06271) (with which both files finish in ~3s in Chrome Canary and ~4s in Firefox).\n\n</details>\n\n<details><summary>Reviewed commits</summary>\n\nReviewed at a3127c5 on 9396777, with web-platform-tests/wpt#64051 at 4e761be, using spec-pr-review.\n</details>",
